reference: cjxl v0.12 from .ci-libjxl/tools/cjxl.

THE CONTROL THAT MAKES THIS COMPARABLE: the cjxl arm was RE-MEASURED in the
same run, and it lands within 1 % of the `_after_` run on every one of the 32
(size, effort, threads) cells — 26->27, 126->126, 1146->1148, 840->841,
4634->4640 ms. The machine was in the same state, so the ours-side deltas below
are the change, not drift. Quote them; do not quote a wall ratio from one run
against a wall ratio from another without this check.

